start-title = What it can do today
start-1 = Opens this window and shows month, week, day and agenda over example data; the example is marked as a preview.
start-2 = Says plainly what is not there yet; nothing here pretends to work.
start-3 = The core (calendars, appointments, series, import and export) exists as a library and is not wired to this window yet; there is no server for it, so the window shows no real appointment.
coming-title = What comes
coming-1 = Real appointments from your calendars, read through the server as soon as it offers them.
coming-2 = Create, change and delete appointments, with time zone, all-day, place, reminder and attendees; series ask "Only this one / This and all following / All".
coming-3 = Calendar list with tick boxes and colour, create, rename, delete, subscribe by link; trash with undo.
coming-4 = Mini calendar, "Go to date", week numbers, three-day and work-week views.
coming-5 = Search, import and export of iCalendar and JSCalendar files with a loss report, keys like t (today), c (new), d, w, m.
coming-6 = Tasks as day items, free and busy of people, reminders through a workflow, a poll for dates from FreeSynergy Decisions.
coming-7 = Planned, not scheduled, no promise: invitations by e-mail, booking page.
coming-8 = CalDAV and CardDAV (sync with other programs): important to us, planned, not yet scheduled.
ctx-new = New appointment here
ctx-edit = Edit
ctx-delete = Delete
ctx-today = Go to today
ctx-why = Needs a server for appointments; none exists yet.
